{"overview":"The rich Baron Von Meislingen dreams of being a poet-- Unfortunately, he has no talent what so ever. In one of his apartments lives the talented but poor poet Peter Långhår. Von Meislingen steals his latest work from him and publishes it under his own name. 'His' poems becomes a success and Von Meislingen becomes regarded as one of the greatest living poets.","tagline":"","cast":[{"n":"Gabriel Alw","c":"Peter Långhår","p":"/3pFUNzN8siRQMD7v31s8R28KPSm.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Manne Göthson","c":"Baron Robert von Meislingen","p":"/zRjXDdzhPW2bOVmhgu8L054diSB.jpg","q":"Q5780746"},{"n":"Hugo Björne","c":"Theatre manager","p":"/q6hebS1XVu15IQsX7OGWSvpqCNL.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Justus Hagman","c":"Old Jens","p":"/uFUTKgebR0m9NVacdYxpKUNETag.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Agda Helin","c":"Rosa Lund","p":"/mWlOBdhd6khYEjeye0qC6PPSwzg.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Sture Baude","c":"The actor","p":"/j32Lvq1hs5mmcQ9EvgcCeeqZFD9.jpg","q":null},{"n":"John Botvid","c":"Peter's neighbour","p":"/iZfi3DCvj9gjhCb0OENh0SEIgCK.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Tekla Sjöblom","c":"Mrs. Lund","p":"/iq3hMYd6Wb4iBBpqSYKfjX5ses7.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Johnny Björkman","c":"Emil Ström","p":"/yTyLAByVAeMr2BaBcraxZMmnjuK.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Helge Kihlberg","c":"Theater visitor","p":"/aHoHrvMnHe9vEoEZ4ENPG8AVoAr.jpg","q":null}],"country":["Sweden"],"language":["Swedish"],"wiki":null,"qid":"Q10594906"}